  <front>
    <article-meta>
      <title-group><article-title>A review of the fictional FOOBAR syndrome</article-title></title-group>
    </article-meta>
  </front>
  <body>
    <sec>
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <p>FOOBAR syndrome is a rare disorder of the fictional GENEX gene <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B1">1</xref>.</p>
      <p>The disorder was first described in 2 consanguineous families with 5 affected sibs who had ataxia from age 3 years <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B3">3</xref>. A homozygous c.100A&gt;G (p.Lys34Glu) variant was found in all of them.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec>
      <title>Discussion</title>
      <sec>
        <title>Phenotype</title>
        <p>Ataxia and seizures have since been reported in many families (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B2">2</xref>–<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B5">5</xref>). Their severity varies.</p>
        <p>Brain imaging was normal in most cases <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B2 B4">2,4</xref>.</p>
        <p>Cataract was noted in some patients (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B2">2-4</xref>).</p>
      </sec>
    </sec>
